          "id": "AALA20260164",
          "title": "Writing with AI outside of classrooms: Secondary Students’ experience with a Customized AI-Bot",
          "abstract": "Existing research on GenAI in education tends to focus on generic tools—such as ChatGPT—which are not engineered for pedagogical purposes. Generic AI tools, however, are unable to channel informal learning towards formal curricular goals. To address this gap, the present research developed an LLM-powered GenAI-bot purposefully designed to assist secondary EFL students in writing outside the classroom. This GenAI-bot, called NexWrite, was customized to align with in-class writing pedagogy so that students’ informal, self-regulated writing was no longer an isolated activity but an organic extension of their formal learning, effectively bridging the gap between outside-of-classroom digital practice and within-classroom instruction.\nThe study addressed two research questions: (1) What impact does this AI-assisted experience have on students’ writing process and performance? (2) How do students of different proficiency levels interact with the AI-bot? The study utilized a quasi-experimental design with pre- and post-tests, involving two intact senior-high school classes of 80 students for three months. Both the experimental and the control group received the same instructions and take-home writing tasks, but the experimental group composed their take-home essays with the support of NexWrite. The findings reveal that the AI-bot functioned as a pedagogy-informed, personalized scaffold, which significantly improved the writing process by reducing both language and affective barriers. The AI-bot also enhanced the logic and linguistic accuracy of the writing output. Analysis of interaction logs indicated that the bot’s pedagogically informed questioning could stimulate high-proficiency students’ creative and divergent thinking during the composing process. The research offers theoretical and pedagogical insights for L2 writing instruction at the AI age.",
