              "name": "Noriko Iwashita",
              "affiliation": "University of Queensland",
              "bio": "Noriko Iwashita is an Associate Professor at the School of Languages and Cultures, The University of Queensland, Australia. At UQ, she teaches classroom SLA and language pedagogy courses, language assessment and testing in the Master’s program, and supervises PhD and MA students in testing/assessment and classroom SLA. Noriko’s research interests include peer interaction in classroom-based research and classroom assessment, the interfaces of language assessment and SLA, and task-based teaching and assessment. Her work has been published in co-authored books, edited books, and flagship journals such as Studies in Second Language Acquisition, Language Learning, Applied Linguistics, Language Teaching Research, and Language Testing"
