          "title": "Item Analysis and Test Equating in the Age of AI",
          "abstract": "This post-conference workshop introduces two important aspects of language testing: Classical Test Theory (CTT)-based item analysis and Rasch-based test equating using Rasch-GZ. The workshop consists of three parts: (1) an introduction to Rasch-GZ, including research background, CTT and Rasch model foundations, and the significance and functions of item analysis and test equating; (2) demonstration of Rasch-GZ and classroom practice (participants may bring their own data for on-site analysis); and (3) a Q&A session. This workshop is practically based on Professor Zhang’s newly published 2025 Taylor & Francis book on Rasch modeling for language testing.",
